## Species-level secondary evidence
- 81 rows, 77 unique species, 4 rows flagged duplicated = same species with a conflicting pathway (Eucalyptus camaldulensis, Opuntia ficus-indica, Oxalis debilis, Populus deltoides): 42 'Gardening' rows vs 39 unique gardening species.
- Gardening species do not occupy more habitat types (habitat.range mean 2.00 vs 2.45, MWU p = 0.437) or more plots (number.of.invaded.plots mean 3.97 vs 7.82, p = 0.271) than species of other pathways; habitat.range has no missing values.

## Temporal context (no habitat column in that table)
- Gardening share of introduction records rose 0.168 (Before 1500) -> 0.446 -> 0.490 -> 0.752 (1985-2019): gardening is the dominant and fastest-growing pathway overall, which is the background against which the habitat contrast appears.
